    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0157" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg85"/>

                <head>No. 56.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Trescot</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 18,
                        1882</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of a
                    dispatch (No. 337) of the 25th October last from our minister at Buenos Ayres,
                    and a copy of a memorandum which accompanied the same, of action taken by the
                        <pb facs="0158" n="86" xml:id="pg86"/> Argentine Government, in the latter
                    part of 1880 and thereafter, in the direction of a friendly mediation between
                    the belligerent governments on the west coast of South America by states which,
                    in consequence of their geographical position, would be able to tender the same
                    with as little delay as possible.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d56-a1.xml" xpointer="d56-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d56-a2.xml" xpointer="d56-a2"/>
